SET: sets is the collection of unique items which automatically removes duplicates or the repeated items 
ex:
set={1,2,2,3,4}
print(set)

SET METHODS : 
SUPPOSE 
nums= {1,2,3}

1.ADD() : ITS ADDS THE NEW ELEMENTS 
EX: 
nums= {1,2,3}
nums.add(4)
print(nums)


2.REMOVE(): it removes an element
ex: 
nums= {1,2,3}
nums.remove(3)
print(nums)


3.CLEAR(): it deletes all element from the set
ex: 
nums= {1,2,3}
nums.clear()
print(nums)

4.POP(): it removes the random element from the set 
ex: 
nums= {1,2,3}
nums.pop()
print(nums)

5:UNION: it combines the 2 sets
ex: a= {1,2,3}
b={6,4,3,4}
print(a.union(b)


6.INTERSECTION:it finds the common value
ex: 
a= {1,2,3}
b={6,4,3,4}
print(a.intersection(b))
